// name :
"P2391220830" "Project Phoenix"
// // requiresfailedtext :
"P0" ""

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - CalvinScott 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P949935449" "Calvin Scott's Suggestion"
// DetailString :
"P196620736" "Calvin Scott told you that it would be your choice regarding what to do with Belladonna. Aiding her would help the Resistance, but having you deeper undercover within the Loyalists would be just as helpful."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - ProjectPhoenixSouvenir 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P3700966401" "Praetor Sinclair's Family"
// tDetailString :
"P3400858773" "Sometimes when you're walking around Imperial, you think about Praetor Sinclair's speech about his makeshift family. It reminds you of the final moments of his group...<br><br><color gold>Project Phoenix</color><br><br>You've been working with Praetor Sinclair since he was first betrayed by his group, and now you would see it through to the end. Or would you? You and Praetor Sinclair split up to track down the final three members of his group, including Belladonna Vetrano. You ended up facing off against her on a rooftop in Imperial City. Belladonna offered you tremendous power if you joined with her and the Resistance, warning that you would lose your own free will if you stayed with Praetor Sinclair.<br><br>Did you side with Sinclair and bring in Belladonna, or did you side with Belladonna and take her offer of gaining more power within the Resistance?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - CalvinScott 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2688366294" "{HeroName}, I've heard about your exploits on TPN. Surprise surprise, correct? Belladonna has told me about all her plans with Sinclair and about running into you. Of course, I could not confide - not even with her - about your operations. I suppose the question here is, do you capture Belladonna or let her go?"
// Answer Text :
"P2217862322" "That would be exactly my question."
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P3903433714" "Normally, I would advise completely against capturing Belladonna. But we have ourselves a very difficult scenario here. Praetor Sinclair is an intelligent man, {HeroName}. I'm sure you're aware of that. The fact that we are talking to each other is already a big enough risk.<br><br>In the end, I can't tell you what to do. Capturing Belladonna will hurt us, but it will also get you that much deeper within the Loyalists. You could do more damage to them from the inside than Belladonna ever could. Saving Belladonna will mean that you need to back away from your position within the Loyalists... unfortunate, but we also benefit. The choice, in the end, is yours, {HeroName}. I apologize that I could not be of any further help."
// Answer Text :
"P4069826421" "I'll just have to figure out what to do then."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Belladonna 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P1789539266" "It's good to see you chose the right side, {HeroName}. Sinclair would offer you all the power in the world, but it would be with you held tightly on his leash. I'm sure you've seen it just in the way he acts; everything planned, everything perfectly controlled.<br><br>I'm sure he told you about my parents, that he 'saved' me from that lifestyle. It's true. He did save me from Hamidon and the monsters, but I loved my parents, {HeroName}. I was a stubborn girl back then, but they only wanted to protect me. That is what makes me different from Sinclair. He had nothing but contempt for his parents. Even at such a young age, all he ever wanted was control over all he had, out of fear that he would lose it all.<br><br>Sorry, I tend to get very... agitated when it comes to Sinclair."
// Answer Text :
"P453939724" "It's fine. But what now? I need to report back to Sinclair."
// Page PowersGuysDead Text :
"P441207658" "Knowing Sinclair, he would not want me dead. And I assume there will be backup coming at any minute.<br><br>We will say that you were attempting to negotiate with me when this so-called 'backup' arrived. They became overzealous and intended to kill me. Following orders from Sinclair, you did what you could to prevent this, even if it meant fighting off the PPD. Of course, because of their interruption, I was able to escape. I believe that's a fairly sound plan, don't you?"
// Answer Text :
"P3487109747" "Sounds good to me. We'll have to be ready to handle the PPD."
// Page Fight1 Text :
"P355526986" "<color orange>You hear the sound of footsteps coming up the stairs - the backup has arrived!</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P3460777935" "(Handle the ambush)"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - DialogChimera 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P3116961678" "{HeroName}. I did not find Belladonna. Did you find her? Is it over?"
// Answer Text :
"P3133707934" "It's over, Sinclair. She's been captured."
// Answer Text :
"P3174224950" "(Explain to Sinclair how Belladonna escaped)"
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P2533147723" "<color orange>Praetor Sinclair lets out a relieved sigh.</color><br><br>It is finally over. Belladonna is in my custody. I will enjoy this, {HeroName}. She will be made to pay for what she has done to me. She will not die; Belladonna will wish that she was dead when I am done with her. I do not take betrayal lightly, especially not when it comes from those who I consider my own flesh and blood.<br><br>You have been instrumental in all of this, {HeroName}, and for that, I thank you. TPN is already broadcasting your victory over this new threat. I will send word that you captured the infamous Belladonna Vetrano, who was trying to become the leader of this group in an attempt to bring a new dark age to Praetoria. You can rest easy now on your new laurels of power.<br><br>As for myself, I shall be busy dealing with Belladonna, along with all the other enemies of Praetoria. Good day, {HeroName}. I look forward to when you and I will once again work with each other."
// Answer Text :
"P3378401984" "See you around, Sinclair."
// Page InformationPage2 Text :
"P609277277" "... I knew it. I should have never had the PPD join us in our hunt. Those men were under my control, but again, as Cole has told me, the PPD cannot be depended on. They are either too zealous or not zealous enough. You did your best in the situation, {HeroName}. You felled Belladonna, which is no easy feat. But, I must admit, you are partly to blame in all of this. I regret that you and I will cease our time together now. We will go our separate paths; I shall continue the hunt for Belladonna, and you... well, you will do whatever it is you wish to do. Perhaps you'll look for more power, or perhaps you'll simple fade into the nightsky of Imperial City.<br><br>Your fate is your own, {HeroName}. I have others that I will be dealing with."
// Answer Text :
"P2640951784" "Alright then. Goodbye, Sinclair."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P4262723795" "Belladonna is no fool, {HeroName}. She tried to distract me with false leads, meant to simply delay me. In the end, I was able to track her and my other two agents down to two possible locations, meaning that you and I will have to split up to cover them. Belladonna will be at one location, at the other will be a decoy. Both of us will have support from members of the PPD whom I control. I will not risk Belladonna escaping, not this time. If you encounter her, {HeroName}, do not kill her. Just bring her in. She will not die... oh no, she will <i>not</i> die, not when there is so much left to do. Here is the location where you will be going to find her."
// AcceptString :
"P1661146509" "Looks like we'll see what happens, Sinclair."
// SendOffString :
"P1390600320" "Yes, luck of the draw. The exact situation that I am not fond of, which is exactly why she created it. We're almost at the end though, {HeroName}. We finish this, it means the end of Project Phoenix, your rise to glory, and my chance to make things right.<br><br><color Paragon>Members of the Resistance working undercover for Calvin Scott should inform him of what is happening.</color>"
// TaskTitle :
"P451748656" "<color deepskyblue>Project Phoenix</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P644929251" "<color deepskyblue>Finale: This is the End</color>"

